  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Aquaculture Cooperatives in MRD Inclusive and Bankable (MACIB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Farmer Organisations and Cooperatives</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Aquaculture Cooperatives in MRD Inclusive and Bankable (MACIB Mekong Project) aims to achieve the self-sufficiency, both organizationally and financially, of aquaculture cooperatives, essentially rendering them &quot;bankable&quot; while fostering greater inclusivity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project encompasses various objectives, such as (1) professionalizing these cooperatives to enable them to play a significant role in advancing the aquaculture supply chain. This involves establishing a robust business model and ensuring a well-structured cooperative organization. (2) The project also focuses on delivering services to member farmers, with a particular emphasis on the cooperative&apos;s role in guiding and supporting members in the sustainable challenges of aquaculture production. (3) Additionally, efforts are directed toward enhancing inclusiveness, specifically targeting underrepresented and underserved women and youth. Empowering these groups and (4) creating a climate-smart cooperative approach (Trainings, CSA practices, and business models) are integral components for selected aquaculture cooperatives. To further these goals, (5) the project engages in lobbying and advocacy, advocating for the interests of aquaculture cooperatives. It also emphasizes collaboration within the sector, aiming to strengthen partnerships and cooperation among stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
